# API Endpoints Reference (HMS)

## Overview
This document defines the complete `/api/v<version>` surface for the HMS backend.
All module endpoints **must** use the `/api/v<version>/` base path prefix as required by `api.mdc` and `api-versioning.mdc` (initial release: `/api/v1/`).

**Write-up alignment:** `write-up.md` sections 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12.2, 13, 18  
**Commercial source alignment:** `hms-frontend/subscription-plan.md` for plan tiers, limits, add-on eligibility, and upgrade signals.
**Primary rules:** `api.mdc`, `api-versioning.mdc`, `response-format.mdc`, `validation.mdc`, `offline-support.mdc`, `compliance.mdc`

## Conventions
- CRUD:
  - `GET /<resource>`: list (paginated)
  - `GET /<resource>/{id}`: get one
  - `POST /<resource>`: create
  - `PUT /<resource>/{id}`: update
  - `DELETE /<resource>/{id}`: soft delete
- Nested: `/<resource>/{id}/<subresource>`
- Action endpoints allowed: `POST /<resource>/{id}/<action>` (must be validated and authorized)
- Query params use `snake_case` and support `page`, `limit`, `sort_by`, `order`

## 0. System Health Endpoints (Unversioned)
These endpoints are **system endpoints** and are not mounted under `/api/v<version>` (see `health-checks.mdc`):
```javascript
GET /health
GET /ready
GET /live
```

## 1. Authentication & Sessions
```javascript
/api/v<version>/auth/
- POST /login                     // Authenticate user and return JWT
- POST /logout                    // Logout and invalidate session
- POST /refresh                   // Refresh JWT token
- POST /register                  // Register new user (if enabled)
- POST /verify-email              // Verify email with token/code
- POST /verify-phone              // Verify phone with token/code
- POST /resend-verification       // Resend verification email/SMS
- POST /forgot-password           // Send password reset email/SMS
- POST /reset-password            // Reset password with token
- POST /change-password           // Change password (authenticated)
- GET /me                         // Get current user info

/api/v<version>/user-sessions/
- GET /                           // List user sessions with pagination
- GET /{id}                       // Get user session by ID
- DELETE /{id}                    // Revoke session
```

